#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707279 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11e722d6-6940-5171-b7bb-72144b59c867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}r^2\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707263} {:answer/id #uuid "122f944c-5603-5199-b661-255b1b22e026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}r^4\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707264} {:answer/id #uuid "741c5c78-5713-5f0c-9bc6-be421b6c5f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}r^3\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707280} {:answer/id #uuid "d32a34b9-0b5a-56ac-9f9b-22c34280bb9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}r^3\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707293} {:answer/id #uuid "eef544d2-b610-51d3-856a-2fca1b6b2f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}r^2\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d32a34b9-0b5a-56ac-9f9b-22c34280bb9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}r^3\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707293} :answer-field/id #uuid "432131e9-efcd-503c-8861-6f99c9367931" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69b12dca-06bc-5890-a174-13469895c360" :question/problem "![Shaded region centered at the origin](images/49/4968facead4cfd2a5ad1b5fd9dd3483e047bbd5b689328177550aa13cab1d4a1.png)\n\nRewrite\n\n$$\n\\iint_D (x^2+y^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}A\n$$\n\nin polar coordinates for the shaded region $D$. Choose the setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge0$ and whose density includes the polar area factor. Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Use $x=r\\cos\\theta$, $y=r\\sin\\theta$, and $\\mathrm{d}A=r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta$.\n\nThe shaded region has radius $\\sqrt{5}$. Its polar bounds are\n\n$$\n0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{5},\\qquad \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nUse $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$.\n\nThe transformed density is $g(r,\\theta)=f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)r$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(r,\\theta)&=((r\\cos\\theta)^2+(r\\sin\\theta)^2)r \\\\ &=r^3(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta) \\\\ &=r^3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required polar integral is\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}r^3\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a914f0-fe3d-5918-9cdd-3d51c8263c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}r^3\\sin(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707262} {:answer/id #uuid "77637cb2-6b5f-5bd8-964c-2abffa6aaaa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}r^3\\sin(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707281} {:answer/id #uuid "777310e1-0358-51f9-ad3a-e965b5b88425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}r\\sin(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707282} {:answer/id #uuid "c3fb11ce-8d59-51bb-b91d-8455030a52ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}2r^3\\sin(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707291} {:answer/id #uuid "e75e8d23-ecc9-5fe8-8676-67d185711e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}r\\sin(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10a914f0-fe3d-5918-9cdd-3d51c8263c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}r^3\\sin(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707262} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c799a0d-d18f-5c7b-8fc0-75fbc8a4b201" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86f884cd-473f-5031-a226-9d4c4da1f042" :question/problem "![Shaded region centered at the origin](images/76/76904d5ed05012b53ed0b0ecdfffd7d71e4f8266fca4e5b0ce3cb07470ba255d.png)\n\nRewrite\n\n$$\n\\iint_D 2xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A\n$$\n\nin polar coordinates for the shaded region $D$. Choose the setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge0$ and whose density includes the polar area factor. Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Use $x=r\\cos\\theta$, $y=r\\sin\\theta$, and $\\mathrm{d}A=r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta$.\n\nThe shaded region has radius $\\sqrt{3}$. Its polar bounds are\n\n$$\n0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{3},\\qquad \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nUse $2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta=\\sin(2\\theta)$.\n\nThe transformed density is $g(r,\\theta)=f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)r$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(r,\\theta)&=2(r\\cos\\theta)(r\\sin\\theta)r \\\\ &=2r^3\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta \\\\ &=r^3\\sin(2\\theta)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required polar integral is\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}r^3\\sin(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707289 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17edbc0b-06a1-5618-92d5-697419f87e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}}e^{r^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707266} {:answer/id #uuid "50888956-62f9-5f20-b3cf-41bbe1a69fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}r^2e^{r^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707272} {:answer/id #uuid "64c50e66-add0-5e36-a935-efd3d4269af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}re^{r^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707277} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c5c062-089c-5fe3-8381-abf9166f910c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}e^{r^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707290} {:answer/id #uuid "c45008c9-66b1-5445-a9a6-542269913c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}}re^{r^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64c50e66-add0-5e36-a935-efd3d4269af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}re^{r^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707277} :answer-field/id #uuid "a996140d-b9ff-5b4b-a0fd-b19e3078d875" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1b917b4-ee92-51db-b189-95995f17916a" :question/problem "![Shaded region centered at the origin](images/30/30d99205fe8a27765fb73f868e7a964a581755095261ddceb8aa45c8e31d60d2.png)\n\nRewrite\n\n$$\n\\iint_D e^{x^2+y^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}A\n$$\n\nin polar coordinates for the shaded region $D$. Choose the setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge0$ and whose density includes the polar area factor. Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Use $x=r\\cos\\theta$, $y=r\\sin\\theta$, and $\\mathrm{d}A=r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta$.\n\nThe shaded region has radius $\\sqrt{5}$. Its polar bounds are\n\n$$\n0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{5},\\qquad - \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nUse $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$.\n\nThe transformed density is $g(r,\\theta)=f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)r$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(r,\\theta)&=e^{(r\\cos\\theta)^2+(r\\sin\\theta)^2}r \\\\ &=re^{r^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)} \\\\ &=re^{r^2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required polar integral is\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}re^{r^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137a57fc-c59f-563c-919d-b67ba96dbbf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{2}r^5\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707265} {:answer/id #uuid "2e6251d9-05f0-5c9b-9546-eba7149e8cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{2}r^4\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707268} {:answer/id #uuid "3591d3fe-ea4e-5136-8bcd-900a93074ff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{2}r^4\\sin\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707269} {:answer/id #uuid "3b795851-dee1-52d0-ab9d-ac8fe8125c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{2}r^4\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707270} {:answer/id #uuid "85ae2cfb-f01b-5885-bf71-f2304060e133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{2}r^4\\sin\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b795851-dee1-52d0-ab9d-ac8fe8125c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{2}r^4\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707270} :answer-field/id #uuid "635ea44b-20fb-5d8a-9489-7774f1b4f02e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb3c45c5-8b7d-54ec-89a6-972052724dfb" :question/problem "![Shaded region centered at the origin](images/5b/5bb0a8fe01c26e5ba9b0112303a2fa4841f1ab07626ca275d33a5a0f59979bbc.png)\n\nRewrite\n\n$$\n\\iint_D xy^2\\,\\mathrm{d}A\n$$\n\nin polar coordinates for the shaded region $D$. Choose the setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge0$ and whose density includes the polar area factor. Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Use $x=r\\cos\\theta$, $y=r\\sin\\theta$, and $\\mathrm{d}A=r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta$.\n\nThe shaded region has radius $2$. Its polar bounds are\n\n$$\n0\\le r\\le 2,\\qquad 0\\le\\theta\\le 2 \\pi.\n$$\n\nThe transformed density is $g(r,\\theta)=f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)r$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(r,\\theta)&=(r\\cos\\theta)(r\\sin\\theta)^2r \\\\ &=r^4\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required polar integral is\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{2}r^4\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63d03417-eb5c-556b-8e3e-71f501713090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707356} {:answer/id #uuid "f11bd925-496b-5f6a-b477-10eaa4830f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f11bd925-496b-5f6a-b477-10eaa4830f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707374} :answer-field/id #uuid "3db612dd-1e25-53aa-8674-179a5112bcc6" :answer-field/key "$C(x,y)=x^2+y^2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c7d1054-bb58-553e-a857-862e42bdd13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707349} {:answer/id #uuid "f4dc0638-cd33-51ef-b54c-bddf9cda81b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c7d1054-bb58-553e-a857-862e42bdd13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707349} :answer-field/id #uuid "4497d788-bbc3-52b0-bca2-0a22fc0ec156" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf A(x,y,z)=\\langle y,x-y\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "180f1a75-b8b5-509a-923d-fb66f0e760d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707346} {:answer/id #uuid "cb7ddf4c-c9cc-59f9-bce7-aa072a75f6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb7ddf4c-c9cc-59f9-bce7-aa072a75f6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707370} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb2ed84-2b20-5cec-9d64-89672056972d" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf B(u,v)=\\langle u^2,0\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "248652e3-f6c5-5073-aae7-554bf75b40eb" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply.\n\nEach input coordinate ranges independently over $\\mathbb R$." :question/worked-solution "The input space is determined by the declared input coordinates, even if a coordinate does not appear in the formula. The output must be a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $\\mathbf A$ returns a vector with two components, but its input is a triple $(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3$. Not using $z$ does not change that input space. Therefore $\\mathbf A$ is not a vector field on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $\\mathbf B$ takes the planar point $(u,v)$ to the planar vector $\\langle u^2,0\\rangle$. Both components are real for all $(u,v)\\in\\mathbb R^2$. The second component may be zero, and the formula need not depend on both input coordinates. Thus $\\mathbf B$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $C$ takes planar inputs but returns a scalar, not a planar vector. For example, $C(1,2)=5$, not a vector with two components. It is a scalar field.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf B$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707357 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8676fb6b-aad9-5815-b176-bd99080aad80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707359} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c5b3f7-82d4-50cc-b11a-c07f8066c621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3c5b3f7-82d4-50cc-b11a-c07f8066c621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707372} :answer-field/id #uuid "59e6458e-cb93-5b4c-b07e-f8691c32c057" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H(t)=(t+1)\\,\\mathbf i+t^2\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707354} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7651a6b1-4b06-5c1f-8652-a982b6598b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707358} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c76ccd-64b2-5506-a2e0-f154c586dc71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4c76ccd-64b2-5506-a2e0-f154c586dc71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707366} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b7ff29-04d7-51a4-9458-73f36041552c" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\sqrt{x+1}\\,\\mathbf i+(x-y)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707369} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e3f6f8-5899-5be8-aa15-012c72bbc420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707348} {:answer/id #uuid "5277db7d-a45e-56d4-902c-8d3940198a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30e3f6f8-5899-5be8-aa15-012c72bbc420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707348} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c59fe5-d8e7-505d-8886-f140971d71d8" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G(x,y,z)=y\\,\\mathbf i-x\\,\\mathbf j+z\\,\\mathbf k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "64bdbefc-9ee8-51e3-93c0-11b6364f721e" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply.\n\nA vector field assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^2$. A formula may have a restricted natural domain." :question/worked-solution "Check both the input points and the output vectors.\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ takes planar input points and returns planar vectors. Its square root is real when $x\\geq -1$, so it is defined on the subset\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x\\geq -1\\}.\n$$\n\nA domain smaller than the whole plane is allowed. Thus $\\mathbf F$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $\\mathbf G$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$ and returns vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$. It is a three-dimensional vector field, not a vector field on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $\\mathbf H$ returns planar vectors, but its input is a single real parameter $t$. It describes a parametrized curve, not a vector field with planar inputs.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf F$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ef3ab76-c3c5-5cfc-8124-aa7a0267a79f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707361} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f08462-ccbc-535b-97a3-9347b2f80a1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ef3ab76-c3c5-5cfc-8124-aa7a0267a79f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707361} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb97b75-254b-56a7-8735-318c6822de8b" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf Q(u,v)=\\sqrt{u-v}\\,\\mathbf i+\\ln(u+v)\\,\\mathbf j$, on $T$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af03f5c8-10cd-54d0-98db-b966d2bae7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707363} {:answer/id #uuid "b2e8329c-08d8-5aa1-b4fe-7d7e90f98af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2e8329c-08d8-5aa1-b4fe-7d7e90f98af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707365} :answer-field/id #uuid "b14b1b08-ab1d-5346-b5f0-37774250ee36" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf P(x,y)=\\sqrt{x-y}\\,\\mathbf i+\\ln(x+y)\\,\\mathbf j$, on $S$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a13252a-67f4-5327-9201-f08da4b2b6d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707355} {:answer/id #uuid "b86717a0-cd9d-5111-85a4-817c3ea37be2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b86717a0-cd9d-5111-85a4-817c3ea37be2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707368} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbe2ec6f-65c8-5920-b355-107d1da50fc8" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf R(s,t)=\\sin s\\,\\mathbf i$, on $\\mathbb R^2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b6d5ec1a-a97b-54c7-bc35-cc60d1536152" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their entire stated domains? Select all that apply. Keep each stated domain unchanged.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x\\geq y\\}.\n$$\n\n$$\nT=\\{(u,v)\\in\\mathbb R^2:u\\geq v,\\ u+v>0\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Each candidate uses planar input points. Check that its formula gives a real planar vector at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- For $\\mathbf P$, the condition $x\\geq y$ makes $\\sqrt{x-y}$ real, but it does not guarantee $x+y>0$. For example, $(0,0)\\in S$, yet $\\ln(0)$ is undefined. Thus the formula does not define a vector field on all of $S$. It would work on a smaller domain, but that is not the domain stated in the question.\n\n- For $\\mathbf Q$, every $(u,v)\\in T$ satisfies both $u-v\\geq 0$ and $u+v>0$. Therefore both components are real at every point of $T$, including the allowed boundary $u=v>0$. Its outputs are planar vectors, so $\\mathbf Q$ is a vector field on the stated domain $T$.\n\n- The missing $\\mathbf j$ term in $\\mathbf R$ has coefficient zero:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(s,t)=\\sin s\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\sin s,0\\rangle.\n$$\n\nThis is a planar vector for every planar input $(s,t)$. Independence from $t$ does not turn a two-input function into a one-input function. Hence $\\mathbf R$ is a vector field on all of $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf Q$ and $\\mathbf R$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "164ff6ea-02bf-5402-a5ad-fb3765f13652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707399} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce849b5-7ab9-58a6-915b-4be34c29993f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707401} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1186e8-4089-5489-a193-f39a0788c394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707404} {:answer/id #uuid "b13001b5-73e2-5e5f-bc13-768bc4abcd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707419} {:answer/id #uuid "fb080b71-5dca-50bc-8d0e-74b882c7902d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb080b71-5dca-50bc-8d0e-74b882c7902d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707428} :answer-field/id #uuid "b71c7fe1-da00-5ceb-bc26-ad14b01dd53f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e55618c-6a4c-541e-bb79-235ed801e602" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{\\frac{5 \\pi}{3}}^{2 \\pi} \\int_{1}^{2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, integrate with respect to $r$, holding $\\theta$ constant. Substitute both radial limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\int_{\\frac{5 \\pi}{3}}^{2 \\pi} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\left[\\frac{r^{2}}{2}\\right]_{1}^{2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{5 \\pi}{3}}^{2 \\pi} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\left(\\frac{\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)^{2}-\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{5 \\pi}{3}}^{2 \\pi} 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate at the upper angular limit and subtract the lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\left[- \\frac{2 \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{5 \\pi}{3}}^{2 \\pi} \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{2 \\cos^{3}{\\left(2 \\pi \\right)}}{3} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 \\pi \\right)}}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(- \\frac{2 \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{3} \\right)}}{3} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{3} \\right)}}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{1}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aa859c6-c31c-53d4-959f-d45b772821b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707400} {:answer/id #uuid "81ddcc5b-b28a-5104-88e9-092aba475ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707412} {:answer/id #uuid "d0019d6d-153b-592e-8875-fe37bb887777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707421} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ddd639-7673-52ce-8622-55c9ab174dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707425} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f4e307-de64-5ca2-a6af-71302a1619be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{8} + \\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ddcc5b-b28a-5104-88e9-092aba475ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707412} :answer-field/id #uuid "d87d0c40-bdcf-5a5a-b212-f92c42a09109" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54ef6dd0-029d-5521-97f3-ebcb0232a775" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\int_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, integrate with respect to $r$, holding $\\theta$ constant. Substitute both radial limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\left[\\frac{r^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\left(\\frac{\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)^{2}-\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the identity\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta=1-\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nThen the angular integral is\n$$\nI=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 \\left(1 - \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right) \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$\n\nWith $u=\\sin\\theta$ and $\\mathrm d u=\\cos\\theta\\,\\mathrm d\\theta$, integrate the polynomial in $u$ and substitute back.\n\nEvaluate at the upper angular limit and subtract the lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\left[- \\frac{2 \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3} + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{2 \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}}{3} + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(- \\frac{2 \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}}{3} + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{11}{12}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707413 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a78194e-71a4-5d7d-ba63-608046fa91a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707396} {:answer/id #uuid "0c21d5ae-cc9a-58ff-99f8-140420b13548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707397} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3ebe2f-687c-5201-9de4-7cd0f4a75d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707405} {:answer/id #uuid "9c530bec-b10b-57f9-9664-97e21f78beb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707416} {:answer/id #uuid "adb12150-11d5-5592-b4ac-7266f917593b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d3ebe2f-687c-5201-9de4-7cd0f4a75d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707405} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa5fe5a8-ca4e-53d2-9971-2d3599dada28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84cb5dad-2ea4-5893-adc6-a25940f878fe" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\int_{0}^{2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, integrate with respect to $r$, holding $\\theta$ constant. Substitute both radial limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\left[\\frac{r^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\left(\\frac{\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)^{2}-\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $u=\\sin\\theta$, so $\\mathrm d u=\\cos\\theta\\,\\mathrm d\\theta$.\n\nEvaluate at the upper angular limit and subtract the lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\left[\\frac{2 \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{2 \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}}{3}\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(\\frac{2 \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}}{3}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{12}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{7}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707415 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03a68a0b-00fa-52e1-b8fb-e607becc1329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707395} {:answer/id #uuid "3135c75d-1708-5ba9-bf6a-e1bbf8f67871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 + \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707403} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba232e4-df50-5dfe-98b5-48721931e2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707411} {:answer/id #uuid "8aed5bd3-2a66-520e-b115-350f14ad2e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707414} {:answer/id #uuid "e4faf576-bfc7-5ae9-9af9-c96eaf9d4d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ba232e4-df50-5dfe-98b5-48721931e2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707411} :answer-field/id #uuid "49ae640f-d625-5d0a-b33e-fa9a2592c58c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ce2c697-bf79-58c5-bae0-6ada2d9c5f15" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\int_{\\csc{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{2} r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, integrate with respect to $r$, holding $\\theta$ constant. Substitute both radial limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 1 \\left[\\frac{r^{2}}{2}\\right]_{\\csc{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{2}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 1\\left(\\frac{\\left(2\\right)^{2}-\\left(\\csc{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 - \\frac{\\csc^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate at the upper angular limit and subtract the lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\left[2 \\theta + \\frac{\\cot{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{\\cot{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}}{2} + \\pi\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(\\frac{\\cot{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\left(\\pi\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2beae8c5-5379-5923-bef3-254ecade9734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707402} {:answer/id #uuid "3ddc38a1-35c5-571e-942a-f4b8071d4656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{8} + \\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707406} {:answer/id #uuid "6a970367-a4dd-520c-a97f-0774a9c3aa38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\sqrt{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707410} {:answer/id #uuid "d77ba180-1596-54d4-85c8-75ed4a5155d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{4} - \\frac{\\pi}{8} + \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707422} {:answer/id #uuid "ff607c4d-4722-574d-8bb2-21d7bfcd339e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ddc38a1-35c5-571e-942a-f4b8071d4656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{8} + \\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707406} :answer-field/id #uuid "4879dfa1-8bfd-5081-a6fa-f67c22afc669" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df02466a-b7c3-58fd-8696-25517b5498a7" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\int_{1 - \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{1} 2 r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, integrate with respect to $r$, holding $\\theta$ constant. Substitute both radial limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 \\left[\\frac{r^{2}}{2}\\right]_{1 - \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{1}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2\\left(\\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}-\\left(1 - \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the identity\n$$\n\\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1+\\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\right).\n$$\n\nThen the angular integral is\n$$\nI=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$\n\nIntegrate each angular term, including its frequency factor.\n\nEvaluate at the upper angular limit and subtract the lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &=\\left[- \\frac{\\theta}{2} + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(\\pi \\right)}}{4} + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{8} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}}{4} + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\left(2 - \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{8} - \\frac{1}{4} + \\sqrt{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\sqrt{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{8} + \\frac{9}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14d06b15-e0ef-5efb-ac67-324ef6787030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid y\\le -1\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707439} {:answer/id #uuid "2a21b008-3c82-5047-a5a4-b9c3d695d6ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid y\\ge -1\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707441} {:answer/id #uuid "68657110-ad39-5a15-8083-3d7f6163d874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid y>-1\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707446} {:answer/id #uuid "69dcb0ce-6202-5926-a112-e0a48567e621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid x\\ge -1\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707447} {:answer/id #uuid "85425055-f84d-5bd1-8550-4ee500fce612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathbb R^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a21b008-3c82-5047-a5a4-b9c3d695d6ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid y\\ge -1\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707441} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c77db9f-ed34-5f96-a629-44f9392efae6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3002c361-c9b3-501b-9b90-6173e7173f25" :question/problem "Determine the domain of the real vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\sqrt{y+1}\\,\\mathbf i+(x^2+y)\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nRemember: both component functions must be defined, and a real square root allows a zero radicand." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, where\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\sqrt{y+1},\\qquad Q(x,y)=x^2+y.\n$$\n\nThe square root is real exactly when\n\n$$\ny+1\\ge 0\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad y\\ge -1.\n$$\n\nThus $D_P=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid y\\ge -1\\}$. The polynomial $Q$ is defined on all of $\\mathbb R^2$, so $D_Q=\\mathbb R^2$. The domain of the vector field is the intersection:\n\n$$\nD=D_P\\cap D_Q=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid y\\ge -1\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is the half-plane above $y=-1$, including the boundary line. There is no restriction on $x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707449 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c76c3c-d25f-56cf-9a6e-5a472ae82495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/0242db9f2ad07e4395012511708f60fb240b1fd6cbcf0d056a0afa05b276ebf1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707440} {:answer/id #uuid "45be9937-34c3-5f06-b1e8-a5d6960823bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8ac3f21f1c73acc3fb218caf12716b3fbbf20568ed896763d3ee1ab9ddc3b8c8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707443} {:answer/id #uuid "4c4a3a95-fe31-56ae-8803-162dcd18e707" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0ec8bb2a7ff212ffc5928984cd6ed38ee36fc0bde69e1d4d5604a2e1d6bf43ca.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707445} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b6da01-342f-58a4-a94e-7f2b677617a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ec7c745c4cf1e295fdfe4d0e5b9b5b47c9b00e2fb5421699d6655acc6d5d169b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707452} {:answer/id #uuid "ab048eed-15a1-513f-ab6b-f7fa6add4898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5e/5e80426064ff9a5fd39f00339cf0047e8e267d227b01eeaa39fa29da2b5799f3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4b6da01-342f-58a4-a94e-7f2b677617a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ec7c745c4cf1e295fdfe4d0e5b9b5b47c9b00e2fb5421699d6655acc6d5d169b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707452} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5886b4f-09fe-5e0c-8581-e04fc59d388e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8597bc7d-4964-5cc0-80c5-4458712ba1d7" :question/problem "Which shaded region depicts the domain of the real vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y+x}}\\,\\mathbf i+\\sqrt{4-x^2-y^2}\\,\\mathbf j\\,?\n$$\n\nSolid boundaries are included. Dashed boundaries and open circles are excluded." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, where\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y+x}},\\qquad Q(x,y)=\\sqrt{4-x^2-y^2}.\n$$\n\nFor $P$, the square root must be real and its value must be nonzero because it is in the denominator. Thus\n\n$$\ny+x>0\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad y>-x.\n$$\n\nSo $D_P=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid y>-x\\}$ is the half-plane above the excluded line $y=-x$.\n\n![](images/40/405d25b4a3d92ce89584a26354a5fd7e55af0ae90d70d865fff1b7575b09c00e.png)\n\nFor $Q$, a zero radicand is allowed:\n\n$$\n4-x^2-y^2\\ge0\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad x^2+y^2\\le4.\n$$\n\nSo $D_Q=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid x^2+y^2\\le4\\}$ is the disk of radius $2$, including its circle.\n\n![](images/0e/0ec8bb2a7ff212ffc5928984cd6ed38ee36fc0bde69e1d4d5604a2e1d6bf43ca.png)\n\nBoth conditions must hold. Their intersection is\n\n$$\nD=D_P\\cap D_Q=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid y>-x,\\ x^2+y^2\\le4\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe domain is the half-disk above $y=-x$. Its circular arc is included except for the two endpoints $(\\sqrt2,-\\sqrt2)$ and $(-\\sqrt2,\\sqrt2)$, which lie on the excluded line. The diagonal diameter, including the origin, is excluded.\n\n![](images/ec/ec7c745c4cf1e295fdfe4d0e5b9b5b47c9b00e2fb5421699d6655acc6d5d169b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a90aa7e-4390-58b6-8a18-daf8461cb492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid x\\ne y,\\ x\\ne -y\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707438} {:answer/id #uuid "48d029db-1544-50c9-bc4d-f9b58be892d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid x^2-4y^2>0\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707444} {:answer/id #uuid "cdbff496-0c2c-5607-aedc-73b55d7ca449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid x\\ne 2y\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707455} {:answer/id #uuid "cfbadf36-8f29-52b2-9e55-c2c9d6ee8cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid x\\ne 2y,\\ x\\ne -2y\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707456} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d4d343-3dd5-5441-a20e-74893a6cc8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid (x,y)\\ne(0,0)\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfbadf36-8f29-52b2-9e55-c2c9d6ee8cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid x\\ne 2y,\\ x\\ne -2y\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707456} :answer-field/id #uuid "dca060c3-ec2b-5814-9a53-34a57ddbe319" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "989d1794-b04d-53d8-bbbe-1e3bbef6b145" :question/problem "Determine the domain of the real vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x^2+y^2}\\,\\mathbf i+\\frac{x}{x^2-4y^2}\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, where\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x^2+y^2},\\qquad Q(x,y)=\\frac{x}{x^2-4y^2}.\n$$\n\nEach denominator must be nonzero. For $P$,\n\n$$\nx^2+y^2=0\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad (x,y)=(0,0),\n$$\n\nso $D_P=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid(x,y)\\ne(0,0)\\}$. For $Q$, factor the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^2-4y^2=(x-2y)(x+2y).\n$$\n\nIt vanishes on either line $x=2y$ or $x=-2y$. Hence\n\n$$\nD_Q=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid x\\ne 2y,\\ x\\ne -2y\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe origin already lies on both excluded lines, so the restriction from $P$ removes no further points. Therefore\n\n$$\nD=D_P\\cap D_Q=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\mid x\\ne 2y,\\ x\\ne -2y\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nBoth entire lines are excluded, even at points where a numerator is zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07250558-c46d-5dc0-aae7-2b4c74b870d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707475} {:answer/id #uuid "c5113b47-6c5d-5aee-a8f6-ed1202372083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07250558-c46d-5dc0-aae7-2b4c74b870d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707475} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc85fe1e-8e16-5eed-83b3-a583d02bb24b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707512} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "776a362e-5a5d-5402-9735-b9408b301b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707491} {:answer/id #uuid "887d6ab8-34bd-514d-9d34-35e11bb57002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "887d6ab8-34bd-514d-9d34-35e11bb57002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707496} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd76a44a-4fca-58f7-b239-543bd79fbe87" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707513} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab46545-0f01-5656-9a5f-c139d7bf503b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707477} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7b5a55-f8a3-5ff0-99e4-a0d58d6f7dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ab46545-0f01-5656-9a5f-c139d7bf503b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707477} :answer-field/id #uuid "f21d3b70-33af-5145-bdc6-3eab6b1abfe2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1e324553-d08f-5dbc-b9fd-80a83282ecb8" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $G(x,y)=\\ln(x+2)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+2>0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y+1},\\ln(x+y+3)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y+1\\geq0,\\ x+y+3\\geq0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $V(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x+2},\\sqrt{y+1}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+2\\geq0,\\ y+1\\geq0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $G$ The components require $x+2>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x+2)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x+2),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $F$ The components require $x-y+1\\geq0,\\ x+y+3>0$. The point $(-2,-1)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\ln(0)$; the logarithm is undefined. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **III.** $V$ The components require $x+2\\ne0,\\ y+1\\geq0$. The point $(-2,0)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $1/0$; the reciprocal is undefined. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\nSelect I only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707494 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "482d1d74-2f4a-5ab9-9281-951a0af4e8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707483} {:answer/id #uuid "92d5b50d-f72c-5d26-b2a8-0a1c93248ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92d5b50d-f72c-5d26-b2a8-0a1c93248ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707500} :answer-field/id #uuid "34d05b28-cad7-5a10-9036-e05c69e9af36" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707480} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7506b157-34f1-55ba-b69d-6943fbc2dca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707490} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8d44b7-53a4-5eab-9e89-5f8432cbb1b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7506b157-34f1-55ba-b69d-6943fbc2dca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707490} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f683d51-6023-5e35-bedf-9fdbd5cbc691" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707503} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3fe546e-4f7b-527d-8b9a-81b00def49a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707519} {:answer/id #uuid "f8fc23b9-d097-53c0-9211-d21779680509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8fc23b9-d097-53c0-9211-d21779680509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707524} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded1cc39-82fa-5ad4-9d02-deb3007dfc89" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "84ce4948-b314-559d-b491-894660b2cd10" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $K(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y-1},\\ln(x+y-1)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y-1\\geq-1,\\ x+y-1>0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $E(x,y)=\\ln(x-1)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-1\\geq1\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $B(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x-1},\\sqrt{y}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-1\\ne0,\\ y\\geq0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $K$ The components require $x-y-1\\geq0,\\ x+y-1>0$. The point $(1,1)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\sqrt{-1}$; the square root is not real. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **II.** $E$ The components require $x-1>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x-1)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x-1),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **III.** $B$ The components require $x-1\\ne0,\\ y\\geq0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The square-root boundary $y=0$ is allowed when $x-1\\ne0$.  The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\nSelect II, III only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c439e96-0377-50d4-a7af-4895e546b673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707489} {:answer/id #uuid "df0bf835-376a-5025-8812-2c80f4fd9c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c439e96-0377-50d4-a7af-4895e546b673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707489} :answer-field/id #uuid "88ea6a6c-91a0-54bc-b703-cb6847059b9b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707497} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "504b9475-89dd-5a30-90c3-f87bb65635cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707485} {:answer/id #uuid "abcaaaa9-c1ee-563d-a4a7-81074edda576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abcaaaa9-c1ee-563d-a4a7-81074edda576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707506} :answer-field/id #uuid "b33167b7-c792-5521-b8b6-c060924b0d76" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707507} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b225ad2-8aed-5a8a-9ea7-737b8662460e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707488} {:answer/id #uuid "da970778-204d-582c-9661-25ade4a1f096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b225ad2-8aed-5a8a-9ea7-737b8662460e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707488} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f5f3a7-517a-5540-8ea6-e9d6962644ff" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "85c4ad5f-229c-59e7-b9e8-e849af9f5efb" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $B(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x-2},\\sqrt{y-3}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\ne0,\\ y-3\\geq-1\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $M(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y+1},\\ln(x+y-5)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y+1\\geq-1,\\ x+y-5>0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $J(x,y)=\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\geq1\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $B$ The components require $x-2\\ne0,\\ y-3\\geq0$. The point $(3,2)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\sqrt{-1}$; the square root is not real. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **II.** $M$ The components require $x-y+1\\geq0,\\ x+y-5>0$. The point $(2,4)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\sqrt{-1}$; the square root is not real. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **III.** $J$ The components require $x-2>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x-2),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\nSelect III only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c1b8a01-609c-5422-b710-a5e74776cb2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707476} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa05c77-7ba4-5791-b628-2b49cd8e98bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfa05c77-7ba4-5791-b628-2b49cd8e98bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707509} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e6c4b0b-d3d6-53a3-a1ae-0c3be7110cb4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "503ac3ff-1280-5581-a964-6b2b88c76564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707484} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd17165-64b5-51af-a335-d7b2af443bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cd17165-64b5-51af-a335-d7b2af443bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707486} :answer-field/id #uuid "963e1697-bd8c-5ebc-85cf-ad4b91dd6193" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "689aabd2-34ce-5d26-8365-b477bbf95ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707487} {:answer/id #uuid "e41401ed-b2f7-51bb-aa70-f56c68f5eac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e41401ed-b2f7-51bb-aa70-f56c68f5eac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707520} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd5486a9-7074-5289-ae48-7f6b5783515b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c63a2d70-cbd3-5739-9fa6-3418fa252c08" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $D(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x-2},\\sqrt{y-2}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\ne0,\\ y-2\\geq0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\geq0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $N(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y},\\ln(x+y-4)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y\\geq0,\\ x+y-4>0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $D$ The components require $x-2\\ne0,\\ y-2\\geq0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The square-root boundary $y-2=0$ is allowed when $x-2\\ne0$.  The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $F$ The components require $x-2>0$. The point $(2,2)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\ln(0)$; the logarithm is undefined. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x-2),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **III.** $N$ The components require $x-y\\geq0,\\ x+y-4>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The boundary $x-2=y-2>0$ is allowed. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\nSelect I, III only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7edbcea0-a4e4-5b9a-abe8-777381fee67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707493} {:answer/id #uuid "90f22b0e-9022-5c4f-a39b-9b18e0faa36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7edbcea0-a4e4-5b9a-abe8-777381fee67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707493} :answer-field/id #uuid "36da47c7-ffe9-5eb7-b362-ed0c024c8839" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "792d1e27-8754-5c3a-8747-d3c67c4332a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707492} {:answer/id #uuid "e627cd83-a906-5088-8bc6-405c4580471f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e627cd83-a906-5088-8bc6-405c4580471f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707521} :answer-field/id #uuid "98802511-c89a-574f-80a4-e3056aa37bbd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707502} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31a36004-19dd-5401-a5d6-027446d61149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707479} {:answer/id #uuid "3551ec68-1e94-5f4c-8d4a-c69b00acc9e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31a36004-19dd-5401-a5d6-027446d61149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707479} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9007f92-b835-5a1c-8ccc-48bcef6f7aae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0e3935c-9b67-5c67-b0f0-72f2ff2fe2ee" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $T(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y+6},\\ln(x+y)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y+6\\geq0,\\ x+y>0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $M(x,y)=\\ln(x+3)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+3>0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $J(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x+3},\\sqrt{y-3}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+3\\geq0,\\ y-3\\geq0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $T$ The components require $x-y+6\\geq0,\\ x+y>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The boundary $x+3=y-3>0$ is allowed. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $M$ The components require $x+3>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x+3)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x+3),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **III.** $J$ The components require $x+3\\ne0,\\ y-3\\geq0$. The point $(-3,4)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $1/0$; the reciprocal is undefined. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\nSelect I, II only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d472eed-f8d5-5ee1-9db7-ccd243145067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707527} {:answer/id #uuid "14f49d01-9486-5e0b-8026-e0a57a22b0fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true"